#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198093 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198250 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f14ab339-1aa8-51a1-ac86-dc780120657c" :knowledge-point/title "Completing a Truth Table for a Compound Statement"}] :question/id #uuid "4063a7d8-0a49-55c7-9e93-3b7ac58c7343" :question/math-academy-id "e-12679" :question/problem "Construct the truth table of the statement $(A \\land B) \\lor (A \\lor B)$." :question/worked-solution "First, we complete a truth table for the first part in parentheses, $A \\land B$. The statement $A \\land B$ is true if both $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,A \\land B\\,$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ |\n\nNext, we append the truth table for the second part in parentheses, $A \\lor B$. The statement $A \\lor B$ is true if either $A$ is true, $B$ is true, or both $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,A \\land B\\,$ | $\\,A \\lor B\\,$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ |\n\nFinally, we look at the columns labeled $(A \\land B)$ and $(A \\lor B)$ to complete the column $(A \\land B) \\lor (A \\lor B)$. The statement $(A \\land B) \\lor (A \\lor B)$ is true if either $(A \\land B)$ is true, $(A \\lor B)$ is true, or both $(A \\land B)$ and $(A \\lor B)$ are true.\n\nThe completed truth table is shown below:\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,A \\land B\\,$ | $\\, A \\lor B\\,$ | $\\,(A \\land B) \\lor (A \\lor B) \\,$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm T}$ |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm T}$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm T}$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm F}$ |"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198094 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198251 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bbe7854c-d438-5ee0-adc8-c32d5d800050" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying a Compound Statement"}] :question/id #uuid "e46add42-b23d-59cc-a611-a2f1b282d3bb" :question/math-academy-id "e-12701" :question/problem "Simplify the statement $P \\land (Q \\lor Q)$." :question/worked-solution "The expression $Q \\lor Q$ simplifies to just $Q$.\n\nSo, the given statement can be simplified to\n$P \\land Q$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198095 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198249 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "21fd31e7-1eed-5dad-aff2-691ba1737b92" :knowledge-point/title "Completing a Truth Table"}] :question/id #uuid "e94e320d-c2d0-5ab4-b1e5-4e1e2c667bd5" :question/math-academy-id "e-12703" :question/problem "What are the missing entries in the following truth table?\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,A \\land B\\,$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\phantom{F}}$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\phantom{F}}$ |" :question/worked-solution "The statement $A \\land B$ is true if both $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\nThe complete truth table is shown below:\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,A \\land B\\,$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm F}$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm F}$ |"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570759 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198251 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bbe7854c-d438-5ee0-adc8-c32d5d800050" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying a Compound Statement"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34373780-153a-5776-ad52-5d02082ccfa8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(Q∨R)∧P" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570217} {:answer/id #uuid "a2ff27c5-aae1-51e9-a0ad-5495650e14ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Q∨(R∧P)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570412} {:answer/id #uuid "a6aa55a2-920e-5757-b09a-bb0b60c1b87f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(Q∨R)∨P" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570420} {:answer/id #uuid "bc9b4799-d2cc-5344-899c-412f238124d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Q∨R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570457} {:answer/id #uuid "e33e1c64-3e75-51e2-a69d-9f41040a8281" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(Q∧P)∨R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570521}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "34373780-153a-5776-ad52-5d02082ccfa8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(Q∨R)∧P" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570217} :answer-field/id #uuid "f0c6bb96-b4df-5b06-b40b-3a6a8adba71d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570689}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "974d976d-65a4-5d23-86e7-77e1c81632fd" :question/math-academy-id "q-170781" :question/problem "Simplify the statement $(Q∨R)∧(P∨P).$" :question/worked-solution "Th